    "diff_hunk": "@@ -385,109 +385,94 @@ interpreted as a language tag. Validity or well-formedness are not enforced. [[!\n <h3 id=resources>Resources</h3>\n \n <div algorithm>\n-<p>The <dfn>fetch steps</dfn> for a given <a for=/>notification</a> <var>notification</var> are:\n+<p>The <dfn>fetch steps</dfn>, given a <a for=/>notification</a> <var>notification</var> and null or\n+an <a for=/>environment settings object</a> <var>settings</var>, are:\n \n <ol>\n- <!-- XXX image fetching is underspecified: https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/4474 -->\n- <li>\n-  <p>If the notification platform supports images, <a for=/>fetch</a>\n-  <var>notification</var>'s <a>image URL</a>, if <a>image URL</a> is set.\n-\n-  <p class=note>The intent is to fetch this resource similar to an\n-  <a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#update-the-image-data\"><code>&lt;img&gt;</code></a>,\n-  but this <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=24055\">needs abstracting</a>.\n-\n-  <p>Then, <a>in parallel</a>:\n-\n-  <ol>\n-   <li><p>Wait for the <a for=/>response</a>.\n+ <li><p>If the notification platform supports images and <var>notification</var>'s\n+ <a for=notification>image URL</a> is set, then <a>fetch a notification resource</a> given\n+ <var>notification</var>, <var>notification</var>'s <a for=notification>image URL</a>,\n+ <var>settings</var>, and the following step given a resource <var>resource</var>: set\n+ <var>notification</var>'s <a for=notification>image resource</a> to <var>resource</var>.\n+\n+ <li><p>If the notification platform supports icons and <var>notification</var>'s\n+ <a for=notification>icon URL</a> is set, then <a>fetch a notification resource</a> given\n+ <var>notification</var>, <var>notification</var>'s <a for=notification>icon URL</a>,\n+ <var>settings</var>, and the following step given a resource <var>resource</var>: set\n+ <var>notification</var>'s <a for=notification>icon resource</a> to <var>resource</var>.\n+\n+ <li><p>If the notification platform supports badges and <var>notification</var>'s\n+ <a for=notification>badge URL</a> is set, then <a>fetch a notification resource</a> given\n+ <var>notification</var>, <var>notification</var>'s <a for=notification>badge URL</a>,\n+ <var>settings</var>, and the following step given a resource <var>resource</var>: set\n+ <var>notification</var>'s <a for=notification>badge resource</a> to <var>resource</var>.\n+\n+ <li><p>If the notification platform supports actions and action icons, then\n+ <a for=list>for each</a> <var>action</var> of <var>notification</var>'s\n+ <a for=notification>actions</a>: if <var>action</var>'s <a for=\"notification action\">icon URL</a>\n+ is non-null, then <a>fetch a notification resource</a> given <var>notification</var>,\n+ <var>action</var>'s <a for=\"notification action\">icon URL</a>, <var>settings</var>, and the\n+ following step given a resource <var>resource</var>: set <var>action</var>'s\n+ <a for=\"notification action\">icon resource</a> to <var>resource</var>.\n+</ol>\n+</div>\n \n-   <li><p>If the <a for=/>response</a>'s <a>internal response</a>'s <a for=response>type</a> is\n-   \"<code>default</code>\", then attempt to decode the resource as image.\n+<div algorithm>\n+<p>To <dfn>fetch a notification resource</dfn>, given a <a for=/>notification</a>\n+<var>notification</var>, a <a for=/>URL</a> <var>url</var>, null or an\n+<a for=/>environment settings object</a> <var>settings</var>, and an algorithm\n+<var>processResource</var> that takes a resource:\n \n-   <li><p>If the image format is supported, set <var>notification</var>'s\n-   <a for=notification>image resource</a> to the decoded resource. (Otherwise\n-   <var>notification</var> has no <a for=notification>image resource</a>.)\n-  </ol>\n+<ol>\n+ <li><p>Let <var>request</var> be a new <a for=/>request</a> whose <a for=request>URL</a> is\n+ <var>url</var>, <a for=request>client</a> is <var>settings</var>, <a for=request>destination</a> is\n+ \"<code>image</code>\", <a for=request>mode</a> is \"<code>no-cors</code>\", and\n+ <a for=request>credentials mode</a> is \"<code>include</code>\".",
